// REJECTS: Unexpected token ';'. Valid alternatives: ['&&', '||', '==', '!=', '->', '['
//
// A derived (qualified) property is `name() {expr}: Type[m];` -- the return type and
// multiplicity come AFTER the body and are mandatory. Omitting them does not fail at the
// ';' as a missing-type error; the alternatives show the parser is still inside the
// EXPRESSION, offering operators, because `{...}` on its own is a lambda and a lambda can
// be continued.
//
// So the divergence is not "forgot to require a field". A rewrite that scans to the
// closing brace and then expects an optional type has already mis-parsed: the type is not
// optional and the brace is not a body terminator, it is a lambda that the property rule
// consumes as one expression.
###Pure
Class fixture::neg::DerivedNoType
{
   code: String[1];
   shout() {$this.code->toUpper()};
}
